@ 29.1.1.1.34 - Tahltan-Kaska-Tagish to Kaska
# citation: Whimemsz, from Krauss, Michael and Victor Golla (1981), “Northern Athapaskan Languages”. Handbook of North American Indians, Vol. 6 (Subarctic), 67 – 85
	Vˀ > V:[+high tone]
	{ P:[-voice]S, {P:[-voice]Š,P:[-voice]Šʷ} } > { P:[-voice]:[+laryngeal], P:[-voice]S }
	[+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo] > P:[-voice]Š (although /xʲ/ stays as such in a few dialect͡s)